"atable or comma-separated)"

msgid "cli.share.flag_skill"
msgstr "skills to share (repeatable or comma-separated); omit to choose int"
"eractively"

msgid "cli.share.long"
msgstr "Link an installed skill from the managed skills directory into othe"
"r AI-agent directories, such as .claude or .codex, and record the agents o"
"n the skill's [[skill]] entry in SKILL.mod. Each destination entry is a sy"
"mlink to the managed copy - the same representation get uses with the auto"
" install mode - so edits to the managed skill are visible through every li"
"nk at once, and a filesystem that forbids symlinks falls back to a byte-pr"
"eserving copy. The manifest is what sync recreates on another machine and "
"what verify checks here; a skill whose entry names no agents stays only in"
" the managed directory. --agent and --dir are additive to the agents alrea"
"dy recorded: --remove is how one comes off. Without --skill or positional "
"skill names the command lists the installed skills for an interactive choi"
"ce, and without --agent or --dir it lists the registered agent directories"
". When a destination already holds different content, share asks per confl"
"ict; --on-conflict=overwrite or =skip answers them all, and --yes skips co"
"nflicts safely. --dir destinations are one-off: an absolute path in a comm"
"itted manifest would not reproduce, so they are never recorded."

msgid "cli.share.short"
msgstr "Record installed skills as linked into other agent directories"

msgid "cli.share.use"
msgstr "share [skills...]"

msgid "cli.sync.flag_check"
msgstr "verify without modifying anything (alias for skillmod verify)"

msgid "cli.sync.flag_relink"
msgstr "reinstall matching remote skills using the configured install mode"

msgid "cli.sync.long"
msgstr "Idempotent and verifiable, with rollback on failure. Installed file"
"s are never deleted automatically; use prune to clean them. --check only v"
"erifies and is an alias for verify."

msgid "cli.sync.short"
msgstr "align local skill directories with the state pinned in SKILL.lock"

